WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.800
We're exploring the
physics of basketball,

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.867
featuring my interview with NBA
All-Star Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.

00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:09.200
Check it out.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.166
A rebound-- in
basketball, you have

00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:15.734
to get a sense of how the
thing is going to bounce

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.734
before the thing
makes that bounce

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.033
so that you can be in the
right place at the right time.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.333
What's going through
your head when you--

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:25.133
how many rebounds?

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.834
Was it a billion?

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.800
I think 17,000.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.400
17,000 rebounds.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.767
The angle in
equals the angle out.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:39.900
So if a shot comes from
this angle at the basket,

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.333
the probability is it's going to
take the same angle coming off

00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:44.433
the other side.

00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:45.467
By the way, that's a law.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:46.734
That's a law of optics.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.600
The angle of incidence equals
the angle of reflection.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.600
Right and, it's like a mirror.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.633
So you have to understand
the angle it's going to come

00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:59.266
off and then the
distance from the rim

00:00:59.266 --> 00:01:01.400
and backboard that
you need to be

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.433
at to have the
optimum opportunity

00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:07.900
to collect the rebound.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.834
Plus, 101-inch wingspan.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.033
[laughs]

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:17.800
Well, it helps, but the
ability to anticipate is--

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.734
So we can spend 10
minutes you telling me,

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.700
I calculate the angle, but
then really, I just reach out

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.900
and grab the ball.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.000
No.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.100
There's some people
that just stand there.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.300
You've got to move.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.767
So you were particularly
potent because you basically

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:35.166
combined your
100-inch wingspan with

00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:38.066
the knowledge of
angle of incidence

00:01:38.066 --> 00:01:39.166
and angle of reflection.

00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:43.734
Right, and what we call hops.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:46.200
What we call hops.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.667
Chuck what are hops?

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.300
That's a new word for me.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.433
In my day, I don't know
that I used that word, hops.

00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:54.233
Hops is-- that's
your vertical.

00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.767
- Vertical?
- Yeah, basically.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.100
Hang time?
Vertical?

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.133
Yeah, yo.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.266
Bro got hops.

00:01:59.266 --> 00:02:01.133
Like, yeah, you can get up.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.433
That's when you
play above the rim.

00:02:02.433 --> 00:02:04.400
You get hops, you know?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.834
He just told me a
little bit about his game.

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:07.633
Ooh.

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:08.867
You weren't a leaper.

00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:10.133
No.
No.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.100
I just-- where I grew up,
we didn't have that word.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:12.934
We didn't use that word.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.367
Yeah, that's called dis.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.300
But I could jump.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.133
All right.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.100
No.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.600
I could dunk the
ball in ninth grade.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.867
So you had hops.

00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:21.133
That's all there is to it.
- Yeah.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.166
So you know--

00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:23.367
I did not have hops.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:24.166
[laughs]

